# Ancient Greːk reconstructed pronunciation — XPF
# Based strictly on the supplied reconstruction table.
#
# Output convention:
#   long vowels are represented by doubled vowel characters, not ː.
#   e.g. η -> eː, ω -> o̞ː, ει -> iː, οι -> yː.
#
# Pitch accent:
#   acute and circumflex are preserved as ˈ immediately before the
#   accented vowel. The supplied table specifies ˈ before the syllable;
#   moving the marker to the syllable onset requires a separate
#   syllabification layer and is therefore not guessed here.
#
# The supplied table does not specify a separate value for grave accent,
# so grave is intentionally not assigned a reconstruction rule.
#
type,sfrom,sto,weight,precede,follow,comment

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Classes
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------

class,front,[ιυηε],,,,
class,front-diph,[ιυηε],,,,
class,voiced,[βγδζλμνρ],,,,
class,voiceless,[πκτφθχξψσ],,,,
class,velar,[γκχξ],,,,
class,nasal,[μνγ],,,,

# Consonant classes / intermediate symbols
class,g,γ,,,,
class,b,β,,,,

